# CASM WP42 trusted reference: casmreloc1
#
# Independently hand-assembled from the casmreloc1 fixture source in
# cmake/GenerateCasmTestFixtures.cmake. NOT produced by CASM. Unlike
# casmrelop1/casmrelop2 (which exist only to prove CASM's own
# classification/recording, verified exclusively via COMP against this
# kind of byte reference), casmreloc1 is the vehicle for WP42's own new
# verification -- loading this exact file away from $3400 and actually
# running it, to prove the OS's existing aptRelocate loader
# (src/command64/loader.asm) correctly consumes CASM's native R6 footer
# for the first time. This reference only proves the *file* is correct --
# the runtime proof is a separate, later step in the same WP.
# Cross-check:
#   - brain/plans/2026-07-25-casm-phase8-wp42-verification-and-completion-gate.md
#
# Source (no .ORG):
#   - START: LDX #<MSG / LDY #>MSG / LDA #$09 / JSR $1000 / LDA #$4C / JSR $1000
#   - MSG: "CASM RELOC RUNS OK", CR, NUL
#
# START = $3400 (no bytes). LDX #<MSG is 2 bytes ($3400-$3401, immediate,
# low-byte extraction -- never relocatable). LDY #>MSG is 2 bytes
# ($3402-$3403, immediate, high-byte extraction -- the fixture's one
# relocatable entry). LDA #$09 is 2 bytes ($3404-$3405, DOS_PRINT_STR,
# a plain constant, never relocatable). JSR $1000 is 3 bytes
# ($3406-$3408, OS_API, a plain numeric literal, never relocatable).
# LDA #$4C is 2 bytes ($3409-$340A, DOS_EXIT). JSR $1000 is 3 bytes
# ($340B-$340D). MSG = $340E (immediately after): high byte $34, low
# byte $0E. Program offset (CasmPc - $3400): LDY #>MSG's ValLo=3.
#
# Hand assembly:
#   00 34              PRG load-address header ($3400, little-endian)
#   A2 0E              LDX #$0E                     (MSG's low byte)
#   A0 34              LDY #$34                     (MSG's high byte)
#   A9 09              LDA #$09                     (DOS_PRINT_STR)
#   20 00 10           JSR $1000                    (OS_API)
#   A9 4C              LDA #$4C                     (DOS_EXIT)
#   20 00 10           JSR $1000                    (OS_API)
#   43 41 53 4D 20     .BYTE "CASM "
#   52 45 4C 4F 43 20  .BYTE "RELOC "
#   52 55 4E 53 20     .BYTE "RUNS "
#   4F 4B              .BYTE "OK"
#   0D 00              .BYTE CR, NUL
#   03 00              R6 table entry: offset 3 (LDY #>MSG's extracted byte)
#   00 34              R6 footer: base address ($3400, little-endian)
#   01 00              R6 footer: relocation entry count (1)
#   52 36              R6 footer: ASCII magic "R6"
#
# bytes: 44
# sha256: f888ce5af9343849705b7c375fa51c0bd841d50461e7271f7e9c112006940654

